---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"wdctl\")"
---
Show hardware watchdog status

Usage: wdctl [OPTIONS] [DEVICES]...

Arguments:
  [DEVICES]...  Devices to query. With none, /dev/watchdog0 is used

Options:
  -d, --device <PATH>  Watchdog device path (default: /dev/watchdog0)
  -I, --noident        Don't print the identity and device line
  -F, --noflags        Don't print the table of feature and status flags
  -T, --notimeouts     Don't print the timeout block
  -x, --flags-only     Print only the flags table (suppress identity and timeouts)
  -n, --noheadings     Don't print the flags-table header row
  -h, --help           Print help
  -V, --version        Print version
